==Scythe and Fang Changes==
We laid out our intentions to rebalance Osmumten's Fang and the Scythe of Vitur [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/project-rebalance-overview-scythe--fang?oldschool=1 back in December], and today, these changes are going live! Here’s a refresher.

===Osmumten's Fang===
We know the Old School community ''love ''efficiency, but after Desert Treasure II, this weapon became a little ''too ''efficient – its Slash bonus was comparable to that of much stronger weapons that require serious upkeep!

We’ve decided to solidify the Fang as a Stab weapon by removing its double Accuracy roll effect from the Slash combat style. This means that you’ll ''only ''see the Fang’s benefits while using it to Stab.

This change lets Slash weapons like the Blade of Saeldor and the Scythe of Vitur really shine, making them a worthy investment once more.

Speaking of the Scythe…

===Scythe of Vitur===
We've buffed the Scythe! 

First up, we’ve added +15 Slash Accuracy, which in current use cases increases the Scythe’s DPS anywhere between 0.2% for low-defence bosses (like the big nylocas) and 7% for higher-defence encounters (like General Graardor).

We’ve also made big changes to how you charge the Scythe. For one thing, charges are now cheaper at one Vial of Blood and 200 Blood Runes for 100 charges. That’s a 100 Blood Rune discount!

Additionally, charges are now only used when the Scythe rolls at least one hit above 0. No more burning through your charges without even hitting the enemy! While the Scythe’s new Accuracy buff means you won’t be rolling 0s as often, this change will help out where you need it most – fighting big, high-defence NPCs!

We’ve pushed these two updates out in advance of the rest of Project Rebalance so that you can reap the benefits of these much-requested changes earlier. Don’t worry – we’re still working on the rest and hope to share more news with you soon.

==Jagex Launcher Update==
On Thursday January 18th, the Jagex Launcher will be undergoing maintenance for general security improvements. The exact time will be posted via our social channels and shared on the [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/game-status-information-centre?oldschool=1 Game Status page]. We don't expect there to be any downtime.

As part of this, players will be required to log back into the Launcher with a [https://www.jagex.com/en-GB/accounts Jagex Account.]

If you are already playing via the Launcher, you will be able to continue playing until you either log out or attempt to change world. After this, you will then be required to log back in with your Jagex Account credentials.

Those of you who've been using RuneScape accounts to log into the Launcher will be required to upgrade to a Jagex Account. Upon attempting to log in with a RuneScape account, you will see this message:

[[File:Scythe & Fang Updates (1).png|204px|center]]

Simply click on “upgrade now” and follow the on-screen instructions to upgrade.

If you haven't made the switch yet, but would like to [https://www.jagex.com/en-GB/accounts upgrade to a Jagex Account] ahead of time to avoid any disruption, , click the button below and get the best protection for your accounts today. If you’d like more information about the new account system, then check out the [https://help.jagex.com/hc/en-gb/articles/17160273294097-Jagex-Launcher-FAQ Jagex Account Support Centre.]

